     2	# DOS-259 (W2-B): forbid direct `Utc::now()` / `thread_rng()` in the new
     3	# provider modules so they remain mode-aware (clock/RNG come through
     4	# `ServiceContext` once W2-A lands; until then, providers must not anchor
     5	# to wall clock or system RNG by accident).
     6	#
     7	# Coverage: intelligence/{provider,pty_provider,glean_provider}.rs only.
     8	# The wave invariant for W2-A already covers `services/` and `abilities/`;
     9	# this lint closes the gap for the W2-B-introduced provider modules.
    10	#
    11	# Pattern matches any of:
    12	#   chrono::Utc::now(           Utc::now(           chrono::offset::Utc::now(
    13	#   rand::thread_rng(           thread_rng(         rand::rng(
    14	#
    15	# Test files (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests { ... }`) are excluded — fixture-time
    16	# clock/RNG calls are fine. The lint walks each file and skips lines that
    17	# fall inside a `#[cfg(test)]` block. Inline `// dos259-exempt: <reason>`
    18	# markers bypass the lint for documented edge cases.
    19	
    20	set -euo pipefail
    21	ROOT_DIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}")/.." && pwd)"
    22	
    23	if [ -n "${DOS259_LINT_FILES_OVERRIDE:-}" ]; then
    24	  # Test seam: tests pass `DOS259_LINT_FILES_OVERRIDE` (colon-separated
    25	  # absolute paths) to drive the lint against synthetic fixture files.
    26	  # Production callers leave the env var unset and get the canonical
    27	  # provider-module list below.
    28	  IFS=':' read -r -a FILES <<< "$DOS259_LINT_FILES_OVERRIDE"
    29	else
    30	  FILES=(
    31	    "$ROOT_DIR/src-tauri/src/intelligence/provider.rs"
    32	    "$ROOT_DIR/src-tauri/src/intelligence/pty_provider.rs"
    33	    "$ROOT_DIR/src-tauri/src/intelligence/glean_provider.rs"
    34	  )
    35	fi
    36	
    37	# Grandfathered allowlist: pre-W2-B `Utc::now()` calls in `glean_provider.rs`
    38	# that timestamp serializable response / manifest fields. These migrate to
    39	# `ctx.clock.now()` when W2-A's `ServiceContext` lands and the Glean impl
    40	# can take a clock reference. Until then the lint accepts each call
    41	# annotated with a `// dos259-grandfathered: <reason>` marker within
    42	# 3 lines above. Line-number-only allowlists rotted on file edits per
